Z||000000||grinthock||05-07-2001||06:58 PM||||Anyone know anything about California Emission laws?  I have a fiero from Canada and I am lookin at moving to Cali, what do I need to do to my car to make it legal?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jay||05-07-2001||07:03 PM||||Hey, Justin there is a thread on here about the Northstar conversion that got into California emissions.  Try the search.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||05-07-2001||07:43 PM||||If the car is stock, it's a no-brainer. Just bring it in. <P>If you converted the car (i.e. did an engine conversion), then it's iffy. Since the car is coming for out of the country, they might let something slide so check the following out.<P>Generally, conversions are no problem if you use an engine/trans combo that was Federal approved. They might consider CAN to be the same as Fed. Fed car brought into California are accepted. You need to ask.<P>What is a no-no is mixing trans types. An NS on a manual is a no-no since they never existed. On the otherhand, they tend to let the mixing of automatics pass, meaning the NS needs the 4T80E, but if you used a 4T60E or a 4L60, they don't seem to freak out. All of this assumes that all other emissions equipment as listed in the Mitchell's manuals is installed and works.<P>A clean swap is good. A mix and match kludge will be rejected.<P>Read this:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.smogcheck.ca.gov/smogweb/geninfo/default.asp?refpage=/contacts.htm&title=CA%20DCA%20BAR%20Contacts" TARGET=_blank>http://www.smogcheck.ca.gov/smogweb/geninfo/default.asp?refpage=/contacts.htm&title=CA%20DCA%20BAR%20Contacts</A> <P>Then call this: (800) 622-7733<P>Don't panic. They are actually very nice and helpful. Give them the details. Don't lie since they won't know or care.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||grinthock||05-07-2001||10:43 PM||||Cool, someone told me something about having to have 2 cats and 2 mufflers or something... True?||||reg||5
Z||000004||WKDFIRO||05-08-2001||02:02 AM||||"Someone" is usually more wrong than right when I hear from that guy..."Someone" once said that the REAL reason that the Fiero was canceled was so that the Corvette could use the nose...<P>2 cats and 2 mufflers? Sure.<P>If you have 2 Fieros.||||reg||1
